('128.21.b.6.H',3,'Synthesizing information leads to:','["more page numbers", "a title", "new understanding", "a copy of the text"]'::jsonb,2,'Synthesis builds new meaning.','original'),
('128.21.b.6.H',3,'Which task shows synthesizing?','["copying a poem", "naming the author", "counting stanzas", "combining ideas from a story and a poem to explain a theme"]'::jsonb,3,'It merges sources into new understanding.','original'),
('128.21.b.6.I',3,'A reader loses focus during a paragraph. A good fix is to:','["reread and summarize it", "guess the ending", "skip the chapter", "stop reading"]'::jsonb,0,'Fix-up strategies restore understanding.','original'),
('128.21.b.6.I',3,'Using background knowledge while reading helps a reader to:','["skip vocabulary", "make sense of unfamiliar ideas", "stop thinking", "avoid the text"]'::jsonb,1,'Background knowledge supports comprehension.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.A',2,'A personal connection to a self-selected book might sound like:','["Page 12 is blank.", "The font is serif.", "This character''s move reminds me of my own.", "Chapter 3 is long."]'::jsonb,2,'Personal connections link text to life.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.A',2,'A self-selected text is one that:','["no one reads", "the teacher assigns", "the test requires", "the reader chooses"]'::jsonb,3,'Self-selected means chosen by the reader.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.B',3,'A response comparing two sources should:','["explain similarities and differences using details", "list only titles", "state a rhyme", "omit evidence"]'::jsonb,0,'Comparisons need evidence.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.B',3,'Which sentence shows understanding of a text?','["I read it.", "The article argues that sleep improves memory, citing a school study.", "It had words.", "It was an article."]'::jsonb,1,'It names the argument and evidence.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.C',3,'Text evidence is best used by:','["quoting without comment", "guessing", "pairing a detail with an explanation", "skipping details"]'::jsonb,2,'Evidence needs explanation.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.C',3,'Which detail best supports ''The fox is clever''?','["The crow is black.", "The fox lives in a forest.", "The fox has a tail.", "The fox tricked the crow into dropping the cheese."]'::jsonb,3,'The action shows cleverness.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.D',3,'A good summary:','["keeps the main ideas in logical order", "copies every line", "changes the meaning", "adds new opinions"]'::jsonb,0,'Summaries are short and faithful.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.D',3,'To paraphrase, a writer:','["adds jokes", "restates ideas in different words", "copies the text", "changes the meaning"]'::jsonb,1,'Paraphrase keeps meaning.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.E',3,'Freewriting after reading helps a reader to:','["skip ideas", "copy lines", "explore thoughts without worrying about perfection", "correct spelling only"]'::jsonb,2,'Freewriting generates ideas.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.F',3,'A student uses the new word ''resilient'' in a response. This shows:','["hiding a source", "avoiding reading", "copying a quote", "applying newly learned vocabulary"]'::jsonb,3,'Using new words shows learning.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.F',3,'Which sentence uses newly acquired vocabulary appropriately?','["The explorer''s perseverance helped the crew survive.", "The ship did stuff.", "The crew was thing.", "The explorer was explorer."]'::jsonb,0,'It uses precise words correctly.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.G',3,'An implicit meaning in a text is one that is:','["printed in bold", "suggested but not directly stated", "listed in a glossary", "found in the index"]'::jsonb,1,'Implicit meaning must be inferred.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.H',3,'In a response to a principal, the most appropriate register is:','["slangy and joking", "whispered", "formal and respectful", "rude and short"]'::jsonb,2,'Register should fit the audience.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.H',3,'A friendly text to a classmate about homework might use:','["a bibliography", "legal terms", "archaic words", "informal vocabulary and a relaxed tone"]'::jsonb,3,'Informal tone suits peers.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.I',3,'When new evidence contradicts an earlier response, a reader should:','["adjust the response to fit the evidence", "ignore the evidence", "repeat the old answer", "delete the text"]'::jsonb,0,'Good thinkers revise.','original'),
('128.21.b.7.I',3,'Reflecting on a response means:','["skipping notes", "thinking about whether it still makes sense", "guessing again", "ending the reading"]'::jsonb,1,'Reflection improves responses.','original'),
('128.21.b.8.A',3,'Themes across two stories are best inferred by:','["counting characters", "ignoring events", "comparing text evidence from both", "reading only titles"]'::jsonb,2,'Evidence reveals shared themes.','original'),
('128.21.b.8.B',3,'A character''s internal response is:','["the title", "the setting", "a spoken line only", "a thought or feeling inside the character"]'::jsonb,3,'Internal responses are thoughts or feelings.','original'),
