('128.21.b.9.C',3,'A playwright shows what a character is like through:','["an index", "dialogue and staging", "a table of contents", "footnotes"]'::jsonb,1,'Dialogue and staging reveal character.','original'),
('128.21.b.9.C',3,'Stage directions help actors by:','["teaching grammar", "hiding lines", "describing movement and tone", "listing sources"]'::jsonb,2,'They guide performance.','original'),
('128.21.b.9.D.i',3,'A controlling idea or thesis is best supported by:','["long quotes with no explanation", "unrelated stories", "guesses", "relevant evidence"]'::jsonb,3,'Evidence supports the thesis.','original'),
('128.21.b.9.D.i',3,'Where would a reader usually find a thesis?','["in the introduction", "in the index", "on the cover", "in the glossary"]'::jsonb,0,'The thesis typically appears early.','original'),
